\end{equation*}
so that on the interval $0\le z\le h$
\begin{equation*}
\psi(z)=\bigl(A+Bz\bigr)\cosh kz+\bigl(C+Dz\bigr)\sinh kz .
\end{equation*}
The no-slip condition at the free surface is $U(0)=0$, i.e. $\psi'(0)=0$,
and the kinematic condition in the steady state is $W(0)=0$, i.e.
$\psi(0)=0$.  With $\psi(0)=0$

\begin{equation*}
\psi(z)=Bz\cosh kz+\bigl(Dz-C_{0}\bigr)\sinh kz ,
\end{equation*}
and $\psi'(0)=0$ gives $C_{0}=B/k$.  Hence, with
$C_{h}=\cosh kh$, $S_{h}=\sinh kh$,

